        "original_id": "b7cd4110-48fa-5d95-9894-c85f5af45d34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Gettysburg, Battle of Tarawa\n- Places: Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, Pacific Theater of World War II, Pennsylvania Route 134, cemetery consecration site\n- Topics: American Civil War, Gettysburg Address\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Gettysburg was fought on July 1–3, 1863, in and around Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, by Union and Confederate forces during the American Civil War.\n- Pennsylvania Route 134 was used during the 1863 Battle of Gettysburg for the procession to the cemetery consecration where the Gettysburg Address was delivered.\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought on 20–23 November 1943 in the Pacific Theater of World War II.",
